hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"232","On divorce: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Awf, from Anas ibn Sirin, who said: It reached me that Abu Ayyub - meaning he intended to divorce Umm Ayyub - consulted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Divorcing Umm Ayyub is a grave sin."
"233","Ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, that Ghaylan ibn Salamah embraced Islam while having ten wives, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to keep four of them."
"234","Muhammad ibn Khallad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj; Ata informed me, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining of her husband, and he said: Will you return his garden to him? She said: Yes, and more. He said: As for the more, no."
"235","Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us. He said: And Dawud ibn Abi Asim said: He informed that Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed him that a woman who was under Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas - and he had given her a garden as dower, and he was jealous, so he struck her and broke her hand - came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained of him to him, and said: I shall return his garden to him. So he called her husband and said: She returns your garden to you. He said: And is that mine? He said: Yes. He said: I have accepted, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go, and it is one. Then she married al-Rifa'ah al-Amiri after him, and he struck her, so she came to Uthman and said: I shall return his dower to him. So Uthman called him and he accepted, and Uthman said: Go, and it is one."
"236","Ishaq ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning a woman who seeks khul': He shall not take from her more than he gave her."
"237","Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking from a woman who seeks khul' more than he gave her. Abu Dawud said: Waki said: I asked Ibn Jurayj about it, [and he denied it and did not recognize it]."
